upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/turnstile-spin
verified: 2026-09-29
scope: directory
reason: Deliberate secret-handling and scope hardening over upstream (compared against upstream 5cd3c5d1, 2026-09-05). New-widget flow never lets the secret enter the agent process: widget-create.sh discards the one-time secret and returns only status/sitekey/secret_configuration, the user stores TURNSTILE_SECRET directly, and validate.sh is not run for new widgets (upstream captures the secret from `wrangler turnstile widget create --json` or the helper and pipes it through validate.sh). Step 6 adds a fail-closed existing-backend boundary; references/vanilla-html.md and references/hugo.md drop upstream's "add a Pages Function / Worker / third-party form host" options and the `pages secret put` pipe. Local-only files kept on purpose: scripts/fetch-secret.sh (metadata-only existing-widget lookup), scripts/worker-deploy.sh (fail-closed stub, exits 2 with extra_infrastructure_out_of_scope), templates/worker/ (historical upstream artifact, marked archived, never invoked). tests/validation.md is rewritten to match (bin/turnstile-secret-test, Test 6).
merged_from_upstream_2026-09-29: removed the non-spec `references:` frontmatter key and restored the in-body Framework references table (upstream 5cd3c5d1, per the Agent Skills specification at agentskills.io/specification). Description rewritten front-loaded with the existing-backend boundary instead of upstream's shorter one.
would_lose_if_wired: A byte-for-byte refresh would put the widget secret back into agent-process shell variables and command pipelines, restore Wrangler-create as the preferred path, drop the existing-backend stop, reintroduce new-infrastructure suggestions for static sites, and leave the local-only stub scripts and templates orphaned with upstream docs that no longer describe them.
to_vendor: Remove this marker only if upstream adopts a new-widget flow in which the secret never reaches the agent process and an explicit no-new-backend stop; otherwise keep as a permanent managed fork and re-diff on each refresh.
